# Start-up and fork keys of hot-text.list that may name a function without a fixed boundary
# (LAYOUT-HOTKEY-INLINE-STABLE; `cargo xtask static`, xtask/src/hottext.rs `check_pinned`). Every other Rust key
# of those tiers must name a #[inline(never)] function. <v0 key> TAB <reason>. A line whose key gained a fixed
# boundary or left the tiers is an error. These keys can still go dead when unrelated code moves LLVM's
# inlining budget; the build's dead-key check and `cargo xtask hottext-repair` remain their guard.
